---
import Service from '../../../../layouts/Service.astro'
import { images } from '../../../../data/images'

const img = images.schoonmaakHero
---

<Service
  locale="en"
  path="/en/residential/cleaning/"
  altPath="/wonen/schoonmaak/"
  title="Cleaning Service Hoofddorp & Amstelveen | DSC Living"
  description="English-speaking cleaning service with employed, screened staff. Weekly or fortnightly, cover when someone is ill, fully insured. Free home audit."
  serviceType="Residential cleaning"
  h1="House cleaning in Hoofddorp, Amstelveen and Amsterdam"
  lead="Looking for a reliable, English-speaking cleaning service in Hoofddorp? DSC Living handles weekly or fortnightly house cleaning for families across Hoofddorp, Amstelveen and the wider Haarlemmermeer area — with permanent, screened staff on our own payroll, not a rotating pool."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Home', href: '/en/' },
    { label: 'Residential', href: '/en/residential/' },
    { label: 'Cleaning' },
  ]}
  heroImage={{ src: img.src, alt: img.alt, note: img.note }}
  ctaLabel="Book your free audit"
>
  <h2 class="h2 mt-10 mb-4">What does house cleaning cost?</h2>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    Every home is different, so we don't work from a flat rate per square metre. Price depends
    on the size of the home, how often you want cleaning, and exactly what's in the job sheet.
    After a free audit you receive a written proposal within two working days, with no
    obligation.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    Cleaning is often combined with other services — laundry and ironing, window cleaning,
    garden care — under one agreement and one invoice, which usually works out simpler than
    separate arrangements with separate suppliers, and you still have just one point of contact
    if anything needs to change.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    The quote shows exactly what you're paying for: hours per visit, frequency, and what's
    covered in the twice-yearly deep clean. There are no hidden charges afterwards — if your
    needs change, you adjust the job sheet and see the effect on price before it takes effect.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h2 mt-10 mb-4">How does it work?</h2>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    It starts with a free audit at your home. We look at the property, discuss which rooms need
    attention and to what standard, and set it out in a job sheet. That job sheet is the
    reference point for every visit afterwards — not a loose note, but a fixed document you can
    have adjusted whenever your needs change.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    From there you schedule a weekly or fortnightly visit at a time that suits you, plus a deep
    clean twice a year that picks up the spots a regular round doesn't reach.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    Every visit lands in your own calendar — we sync to Google, Outlook and Apple, so you never
    have to guess which day it is and see the moment we reschedule anything. A single dedicated
    account manager is your only point of contact: requests and changes come to us, never to the
    person standing in your kitchen.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h2 mt-10 mb-4">What's included?</h2>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    Kitchens, bathrooms, floors, surfaces, dusting and bins — room by room, to your job sheet.
    Want extras like the inside of the oven, the fridge, or interior windows? Those are agreed in
    advance, so there's never any ambiguity about what is and isn't done.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    For <a href="/en/residential/window-cleaning/" class="text-accent hover:underline">exterior window cleaning</a> and
    <a href="/en/residential/garden/" class="text-accent hover:underline">garden care</a> we run
    separate, specialised services — also arrangeable under the same agreement, so you're not
    left juggling multiple suppliers and multiple invoices.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    Not happy with something specific? You have 48 hours to tell us and we redo it at no charge —
    and walk the job sheet with you in case it's the specification, not the execution, that needs
    adjusting.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h2 mt-10 mb-4">Who comes into your home?</h2>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    Everyone who cleans for you is employed by DSC Living, on a Dutch employment contract — no
    rotating freelancers, no subcontracting. Everyone is screened before their first visit, and
    you're told in advance who's coming. If someone is ill or on holiday, we arrange cover
    without you having to chase it.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    Our work is covered by business liability insurance, so if something is damaged, it's
    replaced. More on how we screen staff and handle keys is on our
    <a href="/en/safety/" class="text-accent hover:underline">safety and security</a> page.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    That's a different starting point from hiring a cleaner directly through a listing or a
    social media group. In that case, Dutch law generally treats you as the employer — with the
    obligations that carries, even without a written contract. With DSC Living, you have a
    supplier and an invoice, and those obligations sit with us.
  </p>

  <h2 class="h2 mt-10 mb-4">Which areas do we work in?</h2>
  <p class="body-copy mb-4">
    We provide house cleaning in Hoofddorp, Amstelveen and the wider Haarlemmermeer area, and we
    also work in Amsterdam. Not sure your address falls inside our service area? Send us a
    message — we usually know within a few minutes.
  </p>
  <p class="body-copy">
    Cleaning is one of six services you can combine under a single contract. A full overview,
    including laundry and ironing, organising, garden, cooking and car care, is on the
    <a href="/en/residential/" class="text-accent hover:underline">residential page</a>.
  </p>
</Service>
